# Phase 6, the stuck detector in a fleet: a worker with no progress note for
# twice the time is told to its leader, ten minutes later to the
# orchestrator, ten minutes later to the person as an item, and a progress
# note clears it: the item is withdrawn.
agent G1.1: listen
agent B1.1: hang
file brief.md: Target: the shop | Change: your part | Constraints: none | Ownership: your own files | Acceptance: the check passes
git
orch: init
human: set fleets.mode on
orch: run new "the shop, by fleets"                 -> expect r1
task G1 "Build billing" --name "billing one" --fleet billing --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
orch: start G1                                      -> expect "(G1.1)"
as-worker G1.1: task add B1 "Refunds" --name "refund flow" --owns refunds.txt --check "exit 0" --brief brief.md
as-worker G1.1: start B1                            -> expect "(B1.1)"
term-event working r2/B1.1
clock +31m
as-worker G1.1: status --sweep --quiet
term-event working r2/B1.1
clock +30m
as-worker G1.1: status --sweep --quiet
as-worker G1.1: wait --timeout 0                    -> expect stuck B1 "no progress note"
term-event working r2/B1.1
clock +10m
as-worker G1.1: status --sweep --quiet
orch: wait --timeout 0                              -> expect stuck "billing › refund flow looks stuck" "Its leader was told"
orch: wait --ack last --timeout 0
orch: status --items
term-event working r2/B1.1
clock +10m
as-worker G1.1: status --sweep --quiet
human: status --items                               -> expect n1 "billing › refund flow looks stuck"
as-worker r2/B1.1: progress 40 "the refund form is half in"
clock +5s
as-worker G1.1: status --sweep --quiet
assert: n1 state closed; in r2: attempts B1.1 working
assert: no event lost; no event twice; in r2: no event lost
